s a valid solution.\n\n- Substituting $x=-4$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-9) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((-4)^{2}-9) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16-9) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-4$ is a valid solution.\n\nFinally, the correct answer is \"$x=\\pm 4.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186112884 :answer-field/correct "answer-1d3d225d-49b0-5ea5-9d45-ebcfdc91eb50" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdd21e92-2701-513e-b783-bd67ac5e1d50" "answer-1d3d225d-49b0-5ea5-9d45-ebcfdc91eb50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdd21e92-2701-513e-b783-bd67ac5e1d50" :answer/id #uuid "fdd21e92-2701-513e-b783-bd67ac5e1d50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d3d225d-49b0-5ea5-9d45-ebcfdc91eb50" :answer/id #uuid "1d3d225d-49b0-5ea5-9d45-ebcfdc91eb50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233039 :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{log}⁡(256).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the power rule to simplify the right-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{log}⁡(256) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({256}^{1/4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(4) \\\\ x-2 & =4 \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=6$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x-2) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(6-2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({256}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{log}⁡(256).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=6$ is a valid solution." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f312c34a-9866-5b7f-a9d8-bf68bba44d49"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f312c34a-9866-5b7f-a9d8-bf68bba44d49" :answer-field/id #uuid "f312c34a-9866-5b7f-a9d8-bf68bba44d49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1dc865a8-a99f-55ed-b80f-d011253dcedc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed2c6624-a345-5138-8ba0-fd272edd299d" "answer-3b88005d-c042-5ac4-a802-6c3fbb160726" "answer-71fef0a9-d275-50cc-a7a9-2d08bb857707" "answer-150e2764-cae5-5097-b0e0-4013ce39bd89" "answer-1dc865a8-a99f-55ed-b80f-d011253dcedc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed2c6624-a345-5138-8ba0-fd272edd299d" :answer/id #uuid "ed2c6624-a345-5138-8ba0-fd272edd299d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b88005d-c042-5ac4-a802-6c3fbb160726" :answer/id #uuid "3b88005d-c042-5ac4-a802-6c3fbb160726" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71fef0a9-d275-50cc-a7a9-2d08bb857707" :answer/id #uuid "71fef0a9-d275-50cc-a7a9-2d08bb857707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-150e2764-cae5-5097-b0e0-4013ce39bd89" :answer/id #uuid "150e2764-cae5-5097-b0e0-4013ce39bd89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dc865a8-a99f-55ed-b80f-d011253dcedc" :answer/id #uuid "1dc865a8-a99f-55ed-b80f-d011253dcedc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5004d37a-89b2-53f7-9b0b-a8e11a406464" :question/id #uuid "5004d37a-89b2-53f7-9b0b-a8e11a406464" :question/math-academy-id "q-100710" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-52)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12),$ then what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-52) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12) \\\\ {x}^{2}-52 & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =64 \\\\ x & =\\pm 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=8$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-52) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{2}-52) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(64-52) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=8$ is a valid solution.\n\n- Substituting $x=-8$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-52) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((-8)^{2}-52) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(64-52) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-8$ is a valid solution.\n\nFinally, the correct answer is \"$x=\\pm 8.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d66b6ac8-cb80-5f1e-bd76-69c52b0bc30b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d66b6ac8-cb80-5f1e-bd76-69c52b0bc30b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d66b6ac8-cb80-5f1e-bd76-69c52b0bc30b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4d6b80b7-ffa9-575d-84f9-149ac8826313" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3eed8eca-f634-5b53-8c80-0a12204b646e" "answer-4d6b80b7-ffa9-575d-84f9-149ac8826313" "answer-158e7b7b-60f5-5990-bc18-427a015d564c" "answer-1e99bf88-1c60-5d1b-909b-f801215f85e0" "answer-1833719e-2072-5e7a-9cb5-e37a2b744edb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3eed8eca-f634-5b53-8c80-0a12204b646e" :answer/id #uuid "3eed8eca-f634-5b53-8c80-0a12204b646e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d6b80b7-ffa9-575d-84f9-149ac8826313" :answer/id #uuid "4d6b80b7-ffa9-575d-84f9-149ac8826313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-158e7b7b-60f5-5990-bc18-427a015d564c" :answer/id #uuid "158e7b7b-60f5-5990-bc18-427a015d564c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e99bf88-1c60-5d1b-909b-f801215f85e0" :answer/id #uuid "1e99bf88-1c60-5d1b-909b-f801215f85e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1833719e-2072-5e7a-9cb5-e37a2b744edb" :answer/id #uuid "1833719e-2072-5e7a-9cb5-e37a2b744edb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41f4ba90-bf6f-5f13-ae98-77405268cba9" :question/id #uuid "41f4ba90-bf6f-5f13-ae98-77405268cba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-27725" :question/problem "Solve $\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x-1)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(6x+9)$ for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x-1) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(6x+9) \\\\ 2x-1 & =6x+9 \\\\ 4x & =-10 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=-\\frac{5}{2}$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(2(-\\frac{5}{2})-1) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(6(-\\frac{5}{2})+9) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(-6) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\operatorname{log}⁡(-6)$ is not a real number.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the equation has no real solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9bc71c7-9b59-5c65-af5a-72086d309520"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9bc71c7-9b59-5c65-af5a-72086d309520" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9bc71c7-9b59-5c65-af5a-72086d309520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-371b1475-55c5-532f-b34a-de18250ba6b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd4beebd-bb27-5b86-b030-66ca40a0d99e" "answer-792df15e-6b0d-5e4d-9e48-244de04a293b" "answer-dd22f80c-0bb5-52dd-af6a-2e0500564142" "answer-63b5b7ee-a0bf-5cce-8cd4-ef0e8b697d72" "answer-371b1475-55c5-532f-b34a-de18250ba6b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd4beebd-bb27-5b86-b030-66ca40a0d99e" :answer/id #uuid "cd4beebd-bb27-5b86-b030-66ca40a0d99e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-792df15e-6b0d-5e4d-9e48-244de04a293b" :answer/id #uuid "792df15e-6b0d-5e4d-9e48-244de04a293b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd22f80c-0bb5-52dd-af6a-2e0500564142" :answer/id #uuid "dd22f80c-0bb5-52dd-af6a-2e0500564142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})+\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63b5b7ee-a0bf-5cce-8cd4-ef0e8b697d72" :answer/id #uuid "63b5b7ee-a0bf-5cce-8cd4-ef0e8b697d72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡2-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-371b1475-55c5-532f-b34a-de18250ba6b4" :answer/id #uuid "371b1475-55c5-532f-b34a-de18250ba6b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No real solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115941 :question/problem "Solve $\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x+2)$ for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x+2) \\\\ 2x & =3x+2 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=-2$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(2(-2)) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3(-2)+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(-4) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\operatorname{log}⁡(-4)$ is not a real number.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the equation has no real solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186114583 :answer-field/correct 17592186114588 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233699 :question/problem "Given that ${log}_{2}⁡(3x+1)={log}_{2}⁡(5-x),$ what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(3x+1) & ={log}_{2}⁡(5-x) \\\\ 3x+1 & =5-x \\\\ 4x & =4 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=1$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}⁡(3(1)+1) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{2}⁡(5-1) \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(4) & ={log}_{2}⁡(4)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=1$ is a valid solution." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de40916c-8324-553d-9096-bab0579bf8a7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de40916c-8324-553d-9096-bab0579bf8a7" :answer-field/id #uuid "de40916c-8324-553d-9096-bab0579bf8a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-31c812be-9c24-5035-bd82-28fd6df10b9a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4ab6c9e-dc89-5fdb-b731-b962cf7d6239" "answer-09287577-5ed3-56fe-b855-6d26e3c207e6" "answer-4a53b6e2-d85d-503b-9005-7384f32b967b" "answer-31c812be-9c24-5035-bd82-28fd