n/problem "Evaluate $|x-5|-|3-x|+2$ for $x=8.$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=8$ and then evaluate the absolute values before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-5|-|3-x|+2 & = \\\\ |8-5|-|3-8|+2 & = \\\\ |3|-|-5|+2 & = \\\\ 3-5+2 & = \\\\ 0 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e60f0809-006d-5d59-8100-1de6658c3ea0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e60f0809-006d-5d59-8100-1de6658c3ea0" :answer-field/id #uuid "e60f0809-006d-5d59-8100-1de6658c3ea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-18f4ba97-b8dc-5324-888d-a39a7e05bc49" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a07da073-1567-54b2-ab82-80e4aeed8938" "answer-18a638e8-6cda-5be6-a77d-f20d9d4443b3" "answer-18f4ba97-b8dc-5324-888d-a39a7e05bc49" "answer-3cdc4bb2-5d9e-5596-97e3-5781ff5e4c86" "answer-310cbe50-de0c-523d-89e2-0bff3267c529"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a07da073-1567-54b2-ab82-80e4aeed8938" :answer/id #uuid "a07da073-1567-54b2-ab82-80e4aeed8938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18a638e8-6cda-5be6-a77d-f20d9d4443b3" :answer/id #uuid "18a638e8-6cda-5be6-a77d-f20d9d4443b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18f4ba97-b8dc-5324-888d-a39a7e05bc49" :answer/id #uuid "18f4ba97-b8dc-5324-888d-a39a7e05bc49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cdc4bb2-5d9e-5596-97e3-5781ff5e4c86" :answer/id #uuid "3cdc4bb2-5d9e-5596-97e3-5781ff5e4c86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-310cbe50-de0c-523d-89e2-0bff3267c529" :answer/id #uuid "310cbe50-de0c-523d-89e2-0bff3267c529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e848dbc-438d-5d9d-8de6-41c96328b31b" :question/id #uuid "3e848dbc-438d-5d9d-8de6-41c96328b31b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131806" :question/problem "If $x=2$ then $|3-{2}^{x}|+4=$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=2$ and then evaluate the absolute value before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3-{2}^{x}|+4 & = \\\\ |3-{2}^{2}|+4 & = \\\\ |3-4|+4 & = \\\\ |-1|+4 & = \\\\ 1+4 & = \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-52c1e553-d74d-59fd-a539-db479dc23184"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52c1e553-d74d-59fd-a539-db479dc23184" :answer-field/id #uuid "52c1e553-d74d-59fd-a539-db479dc23184" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5cb9b356-5932-53cb-a1f6-0aeb3ef4cb11" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b62c904-4d93-5e91-8fcd-3d63b312cd13" "answer-543e9569-ebcc-52ee-b615-3c6d09b84d55" "answer-d1540b6d-345a-5120-8ab5-0582cc400a53" "answer-5cb9b356-5932-53cb-a1f6-0aeb3ef4cb11" "answer-e404cb10-11b0-59fe-9d87-fdcbd419c82f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b62c904-4d93-5e91-8fcd-3d63b312cd13" :answer/id #uuid "1b62c904-4d93-5e91-8fcd-3d63b312cd13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543e9569-ebcc-52ee-b615-3c6d09b84d55" :answer/id #uuid "543e9569-ebcc-52ee-b615-3c6d09b84d55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1540b6d-345a-5120-8ab5-0582cc400a53" :answer/id #uuid "d1540b6d-345a-5120-8ab5-0582cc400a53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cb9b356-5932-53cb-a1f6-0aeb3ef4cb11" :answer/id #uuid "5cb9b356-5932-53cb-a1f6-0aeb3ef4cb11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e404cb10-11b0-59fe-9d87-fdcbd419c82f" :answer/id #uuid "e404cb10-11b0-59fe-9d87-fdcbd419c82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b8991b67-f1ef-53f9-975f-0551777dc4d1" :question/id #uuid "b8991b67-f1ef-53f9-975f-0551777dc4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-212313" :question/problem "If $x=1,$ then $3-|{2}^{-x}-\\frac{5}{2}|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=1$ and then evaluate the absolute value before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-|{2}^{-x}-\\frac{5}{2}| & = \\\\ 3-|{2}^{-1}-\\frac{5}{2}| & = \\\\ 3-|\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{2}| & = \\\\ 3-|-2| & = \\\\ 3-2 & = \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4149acf6-bd2b-5cdb-9109-58f31fcedb99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4149acf6-bd2b-5cdb-9109-58f31fcedb99" :answer-field/id #uuid "4149acf6-bd2b-5cdb-9109-58f31fcedb99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-24a75248-37a5-5151-b8cb-0f5575576d3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24a75248-37a5-5151-b8cb-0f5575576d3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24a75248-37a5-5151-b8cb-0f5575576d3e" :answer/id #uuid "24a75248-37a5-5151-b8cb-0f5575576d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f4d3cdfc-97df-54f6-9ee5-ecd71be4d0bd" :question/id #uuid "f4d3cdfc-97df-54f6-9ee5-ecd71be4d0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-215802" :question/problem "If $x=2,$ then $|x+1{|}^{2}-|x-1{|}^{3}+2=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=2$ and then evaluate the absolute values before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1{|}^{2}-|x-1{|}^{3}+2 & = \\\\ |2+1{|}^{2}-|2-1{|}^{3}+2 & = \\\\ |3{|}^{2}-|1{|}^{3}+2 & = \\\\ {3}^{2}-{1}^{3}+2 & = \\\\ 9-1+2 & = \\\\ 10 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-259bb8b7-b747-5b79-8d8c-16284cc398a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-259bb8b7-b747-5b79-8d8c-16284cc398a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "259bb8b7-b747-5b79-8d8c-16284cc398a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-06f530b9-512a-59c4-b8dc-f3b975a5f9af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06f530b9-512a-59c4-b8dc-f3b975a5f9af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06f530b9-512a-59c4-b8dc-f3b975a5f9af" :answer/id #uuid "06f530b9-512a-59c4-b8dc-f3b975a5f9af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a42fde9-ed9b-5e9d-86c6-940fc99b7d25" :question/id #uuid "6a42fde9-ed9b-5e9d-86c6-940fc99b7d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-215803" :question/problem "If $y=0,$ then $|2y+3{|}^{3}-|y+2|=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $y=0$ and then evaluate the absolute values before we simplify the rest of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2y+3{|}^{3}-|y+2| & = \\\\ |2(0)+3{|}^{3}-|0+2| & = \\\\ |0+3{|}^{3}-|0+2| & = \\\\ |3{|}^{3}-|2| & = \\\\ {3}^{3}-2 & = \\\\ 27-2 & = \\\\ 25 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea38a251-ab23-5c87-abfe-28a8670ee8a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea38a251-ab23-5c87-abfe-28a8670ee8a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea38a251-ab23-5c87-abfe-28a8670ee8a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-da4845bf-1401-512a-8c52-28302042301c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da4845bf-1401-512a-8c52-28302042301c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da4845bf-1401-512a-8c52-28302042301c" :answer/id #uuid "da4845bf-1401-512a-8c52-28302042301c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-e6236cb7-b333-595b-87b9-895ea4f220f1" :activity/id #uuid "e6236cb7-b333-595b-87b9-895ea4f220f1" :activity/title "Absolute Value Expressions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049844 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-b0b38d0b-0e33-50a6-903b-f2396119b21a" "step-a08163e8-a307-5f7d-8731-fa1cbf7422a3" "step-d775aea7-e108-5ef4-9f6e-296230133d2c" "step-1b023f9e-0298-554e-be5a-bf787e7e1d6c" "step-3291a708-b56a-592b-9ee3-bf5079c19589"] :activity/first-step "step-b0b38d0b-0e33-50a6-903b-f2396119b21a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b0b38d0b-0e33-50a6-903b-f2396119b21a" :step/id #uuid "b0b38d0b-0e33-50a6-903b-f2396119b21a" :step/content "question-68630caf-af8f-50ee-bc03-18c9657f8cb4" :step/next "step-a08163e8-a307-5f7d-8731-fa1cbf7422a3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a08163e8-a307-5f7d-8731-fa1cbf7422a3" :step/id #uuid "a08163e8-a307-5f7d-8731-fa1cbf7422a3" :step/content "question-3e848dbc-438d-5d9d-8de6-41c96328b31b" :step/next "step-d775aea7-e108-5ef4-9f6e-296230133d2c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d775aea7-e108-5ef4-9f6e-296230133d2c" :step/id #uuid "d775aea7-e108-5ef4-9f6e-296230133d2c" :step/content "question-b8991b67-f1ef-53f9-975f-0551777dc4d1" :step/next "step-1b023f9e-0298-554e-be5a-bf787e7e1d6c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b023f9e-0298-554e-be5a-bf787e7e1d6c" :step/id #uuid "1b023f9e-0298-554e-be5a-bf787e7e1d6c" :step/content "question-f4d3cdfc-97df-54f6-9ee5-ecd71be4d0bd" :step/next "step-3291a708-b56a-592b-9ee3-bf5079c19589" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3291a708-b56a-592b-9ee3-bf5079c19589" :step/id #uuid "3291a708-b56a-592b-9ee3-bf5079c19589" :step/content "question-6a42fde9-ed9b-5e9d-86c6-940fc99b7d25" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186135427 :answer-field/choices 17592186135428] [:db/retract 17592186135427 :answer-field/choices 17592186135429] [:db/retract 17592186135427 :answer-field/choices 17592186135430] [:db/retract 17592186135427 :answer-field/choices 17592186135431] [:db/retract 17592186135427 :answer-field/choices 17592186135432] {:db/id "question-cc1f868e-acd2-53b5-a61f-6b065116ee9a" :question/id #uuid "cc1f868e-acd2-53b5-a61f-6b065116ee9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-46386" :question/problem "The dimensions of a cubic water tank are $2.4\\,\\text{m}\\times 2.4\\,\\text{m}\\times 2.4\\,\\text{m},$  where each dimension is measured to the nearest $0.1\\,\\text{m}.$ Rounded to the nearest tenth of a cubic meter, what is the smallest possible volume of the tank?" :question/worked-solution "Each dimension is given to the nearest $0.1\\,\\text{m}.$ So, the greatest possible error of these measurements is\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.1\\,\\text{m}}{2}=0.05\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to find the *smallest* possible volume of the tank. Therefore, we require the *lower bound* of each dimension.\n\nThe lower bounds for each dimension are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 2.4\\,\\text{m}-0.05\\,\\text{m}=2.35\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & 2.4\\,\\text{m}-0.05\\,\\text{m}=2.35\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & 2.4\\,\\text{m}-0.05\\,\\text{m}=2.35\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the smallest possible volume of the tank is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2.35\\,\\text{m}\\times 2.35\\,\\text{m}\\times 2.35\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =12.977\\,875\\,{\\text{m}}^{3} \\\\  & ≈13.0\\,{\\text{m}}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest tenth of a cubic meter." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-278391dd-df9b-5ab8-b856-03ca04c5de44"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-278391dd-df9b-5ab8-b856-03ca04c5de44" :answer-field/id #uuid "278391dd-df9b-5ab8-b856-03ca04c5de44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a64f0aa8-5dbd-5dd3-ae18-7c76124f8c7b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-255bade8-0a89-5de2-8a24-9fd1e2100b17" "answer-31e67d7e-4e60-5f06-8489-9ee7a57c5092" "answer-a64f0aa8-5dbd-5dd3-ae18-7c76124f8c7b" "answer-b6fd67f7-1c22-5e81-be9b-2698dfa44075" "answer-995c6b46-9527-5d81-9c6e-1f7397ab9bcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-255bade8-0a89-5de2-8a24-9fd1e2100b17" :answer/id #uuid "255bade8-0a89-5de2-8a24-9fd1e2100b17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.3\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e67d7e-4e60-5f06-8489-9ee7a57c5092" :answer/id #uuid "31e67d7e-4e60-5f06-8489-9ee7a57c5092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.7\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a64f0aa8-5dbd-5dd3-ae18-7c76124f8c7b" :answer/id #uuid "a64f0aa8-5dbd-5dd3-ae18-7c76124f8c7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.0\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6fd67f7-1c22-5e81-be9b-2698dfa44075" :answer/id #uuid "b6fd67f7-1c22-5e81-be9b-2698dfa44075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.5\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-995c6b46-9527-5d81-9c6e-1f7397ab9bcf" :answer/id #uuid "995c6b46-9527-5d81-9c6e-1f7397ab9bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14.2\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138698 :question/problem "The shoulder height of a moose $h$ measures $2.1\\,\\text{m}$ to the nearest tenth of a meter. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement." :question/worked-solution "Our measurement is given to the nearest $0.1\\,\\text{m}.$ So, the greatest possible error of this measurement is\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.1\\,\\text{m}}{2}=0.05\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the lower and upper bounds of this measurement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{lower bound} & =2.1\\,\\text{m}-0.05\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =2.05\\,\\text{m} \\\\ \\text{upper bound} & =2.1\\,\\text{m}+0.05\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =2.15\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the exact value of $h$ lies between the lower and upper bound, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2.05\\,\\text{m}\\le h<2.15\\,\\text{m}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135427 :answer-field/correct "answer-61ad7ba7-c6e6-5a77-88a2-8f331b4e6cc2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de59b963-7146-502e-8106-8eeb734cdb88" "answer-61ad7ba7-c6e6-5a77-88a2-8f331b4e6cc2" "answer-4c4403cc-a3af-50f8-91d2-7e006f9ca2bc" "answer-16fac51a-9457-5261-b22b-f89d79af0f70" "answer-2e710c8a-03cf-5964-8f07-e6abecb91318"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de59b963-7146-502e-8106-8eeb734cdb88" :answer/id #uuid "de59b963-7146-502e-8106-8eeb734cdb88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{m}\\le h<3.1\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61ad7ba7-c6e6-5a77-88a2-8f331b4e6cc2" :answer/id #uuid "61ad7ba7-c6e6-5a77-88a2-8f331b4e6cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.05\\,\\text{m}\\le h<2.15\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c4403cc-a3af-50f8-91d2-7e006f9ca2bc" :answer/id #uuid "4c4403cc-a3af-50f8-91d2-7e006f9ca2bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.095\\,\\text{m}\\le h<2.105\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16fac51a-9457-5261-b22b-f89d79af0f70" :answer/id #uuid "16fac51a-9457-5261-b22b-f89d79af0f70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.09\\,\\text{m}\\le h<2.11\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e710c8a-03cf-5964-8f07-e6abecb91318" :answer/id #uuid "2e710c8a-03cf-5964-8f07-e6abecb91318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.0\\,\\text{m}\\le h<2.2\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138737 :question/problem "The dimensions of a rectangular floor are $12\\,\\text{m}\\times 3\\,\\text{m}$, where each dimension is measured to the nearest $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Rounded to the nearest square meter, what is the smallest possible area of the floor?\n\nTo the nearest square meter, the smallest possible area is\n{{field-1}}${\\text{m}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Each dimension is given to the nearest $1\\,\\text{m}.$ So, the greatest possible error of these measurements is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,\\text{m}}{2}=0.5\\,\\text{m}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to find the *smallest* possible area of the container. Therefore, we require the *lower bound* of each dimension.\n\nThe lower bounds for each dimension are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & 12\\,\\text{m}-0.5\\,\\text{m}=11.5\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & 3\\,\\text{m}-0.5\\,\\text{m}=2.5\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the smallest possible area of the container is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =11.5\\,\\text{m}\\times 2.5\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =28.75\\,{\\text{m}}^{2} \\\\  & ≈29\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest square meter." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135493 :answer-field/correct "answer-2acee517-33dc-5f55-a0b3-f02e6c6263fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2acee517-33dc-5f55-a0b3-f02e6c6263fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2acee517-33dc-5f55-a0b3-f02e6c6263fc" :answer/id #uuid "2acee517-33dc-5f55-a0b3-f02e6c6263fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b2fa5316-e98c-5047-902c-0d6c438a9d06" :activity/id #uuid "b2fa5316-e98c-5047-902c-0d6c438a9d06" :activity/title "Degrees of Accuracy" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048438 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-59367d0f-feb4-57b0-bee3-c4cdea97ec6b" "step-afdc7c1a-9e06-55c0-8af8-0603e546f8f9" "step-67e2fe74-1f9c-5f39-b367-3beb48c1832e"] :activity/first-step "step-59367d0f-feb4-57b0-bee3-c4cdea97ec6b" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-59367d0f-feb4-57b0-bee3-c4cdea97ec6b" :step/id #uuid "59367d0f-feb4-57b0-bee3-c4cdea97ec6b" :step/content "question-cc1f868e-acd2-53b5-a61f-6b065116ee9a" :step/next "step-afdc7c1a-9e06-55c0-8af8-0603e546f8f9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-afdc7c1a-9e06-55c0-8af8-0603e546f8f9" :step/id #uuid "afdc7c1a-9e06-55c0-8af8-0603e546f8f9" :step/content 17592186138698 :step/next "step-67e2fe74-1f9c-5f39-b367-3beb48c1832e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-67e2fe74-1f9c-5f39-b367-3beb48c1832e" :step/id #uuid "67e2fe74-1f9c-5f39-b367-3beb48c1832e" :step/content 17592186138737 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186107195 :answer-field/choices 17592186107200] [:db/retract 17592186107195 :answer-field/choices 17592186107196] [:db/retract 17592186107195 :answer-field/choices 17592186107197] [:db/retract 17592186107195 :answer-field/choices 17592186107198] [:db/retract 17592186107195 :answer-field/choices 17592186107199] [:db/retract 17592186107207 :answer-field/choices 17592186107208] [:db/retract 17592186107207 :answer-field/choices 17592186107209] [:db/retract 17592186107207 :answer-field/choices 17592186107210] [:db/retract 17592186107207 :answer-field/choices 17592186107211] [:db/retract 17592186107207 :answer-field/choices 17592186107212] {:db/id 17592186110644 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0ed72443-d0d2-56d4-ac8e-61b5fbb5185e" "question-fef83826-7751-5d92-9867-993dd33f1353" "question-5139923c-05c3-5b4c-afc7-050e8c844fa1" "question-81d575e3-b933-5487-8eb2-7aae2b3ca41b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110519 :question/worked-solution "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV = s^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=4\\,\\textrm{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV = (4\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 64\\, \\textrm{cm}^3 .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110645 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4a3d3c61-1d56-511a-8971-a92e96959ca8" "question-c484b581-e8de-5427-867e-86ac0d8ace75" "question-3512c6b0-1995-511f-b3bb-e6f73ca555fc" "question-e83a5e5d-4e50-55da-82b2-166ada387fd5" "question-f8ed5ffa-b9ea-5302-ac51-cfa35a2f9ca0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110520 :question/problem "The volume of a cube is $729\\, \\textrm{cm}^3.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube." :question/worked-solution "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV = s^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} =  \\sqrt[3]{729} = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $9\\,\\textrm{cm}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110655 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-62d14dcd-2286-5ac0-9da8-8fd4144e472b" "question-303cc00a-f8f7-5cb0-b148-e5fe2714f366" "question-20052714-006e-5cb8-9e42-f681fe3b072f" "question-db058a82-1fa2-5274-82e0-1236f8c5f86e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110539 :question/problem "Six identical plastic cubic containers have a combined volume of $48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3.$ Find the side length of a single container." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the volume of a single container: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3}{6} = 8 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one container. \n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV = s^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side of a single container is $2\\,\\textrm{ft}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0ed72443-d0d2-56d4-ac8e-61b5fbb5185e" :question/id #uuid "0ed72443-d0d2-56d4-ac8e-61b5fbb5185e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107260" :question/problem "Find the volume of the cube whose sides each have length $7\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=7\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV=(7\\,\\text{cm})^{3}=343\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7172fc17-8ef7-557c-80e1-19914119c67d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7172fc17-8ef7-557c-80e1-19914119c67d" :