["answer-6c526c14-bb88-5ade-8041-886de05f49a5" "answer-9d4edf44-c7cf-53b5-b877-06a7a5da6527" "answer-92108669-6093-5435-ba79-5169fa05995d" "answer-9a757735-7cc0-5dcf-90e7-545fc78fa434" "answer-d068f486-a976-58d2-8c3b-4190a273dbd9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c526c14-bb88-5ade-8041-886de05f49a5" :answer/id #uuid "6c526c14-bb88-5ade-8041-886de05f49a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4edf44-c7cf-53b5-b877-06a7a5da6527" :answer/id #uuid "9d4edf44-c7cf-53b5-b877-06a7a5da6527" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92108669-6093-5435-ba79-5169fa05995d" :answer/id #uuid "92108669-6093-5435-ba79-5169fa05995d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a757735-7cc0-5dcf-90e7-545fc78fa434" :answer/id #uuid "9a757735-7cc0-5dcf-90e7-545fc78fa434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d068f486-a976-58d2-8c3b-4190a273dbd9" :answer/id #uuid "d068f486-a976-58d2-8c3b-4190a273dbd9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series is divergent" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38c8627e-3005-599a-a37a-fb4e0aa52cad" :question/id #uuid "38c8627e-3005-599a-a37a-fb4e0aa52cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-350677" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8dea3e67-c006-5eec-a9a7-cb2408ce3d5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8dea3e67-c006-5eec-a9a7-cb2408ce3d5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8dea3e67-c006-5eec-a9a7-cb2408ce3d5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b" :answer/id #uuid "725300ba-c2fd-5ef3-8e8b-23e9b44e688b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3922f3d0-9ec0-55ed-b2ff-7790813baa5b" :question/id #uuid "3922f3d0-9ec0-55ed-b2ff-7790813baa5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103114" :question/problem "$1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯=$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{5}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2786ba38-c706-503a-8183-84ee0ea15a87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2786ba38-c706-503a-8183-84ee0ea15a87" :answer-field/id #uuid "2786ba38-c706-503a-8183-84ee0ea15a87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f0d5014-3b13-5aea-b08f-1fb39fc462a7" "answer-8d889743-ce2a-5980-a928-bf56bdaac70d" "answer-ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" "answer-571409cc-60e9-5612-9926-6ed9afcda997" "answer-34b6e35c-dea1-538c-98c8-0094d3f2c403"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f0d5014-3b13-5aea-b08f-1fb39fc462a7" :answer/id #uuid "8f0d5014-3b13-5aea-b08f-1fb39fc462a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d889743-ce2a-5980-a928-bf56bdaac70d" :answer/id #uuid "8d889743-ce2a-5980-a928-bf56bdaac70d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" :answer/id #uuid "ea987183-87c9-5540-a30a-3f341eb3b346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-571409cc-60e9-5612-9926-6ed9afcda997" :answer/id #uuid "571409cc-60e9-5612-9926-6ed9afcda997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34b6e35c-dea1-538c-98c8-0094d3f2c403" :answer/id #uuid "34b6e35c-dea1-538c-98c8-0094d3f2c403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b939d5df-d459-5fd4-9292-d3dcc1c6afac" :question/id #uuid "b939d5df-d459-5fd4-9292-d3dcc1c6afac" :question/math-academy-id "q-50942" :question/problem "$\\,1-\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯=$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /2)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25570059-2136-5352-9294-04bc3533b43e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25570059-2136-5352-9294-04bc3533b43e" :answer-field/id #uuid "25570059-2136-5352-9294-04bc3533b43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d9d7b6b-6fdb-5ed5-bcb4-eab5156b4447" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8085e5d-331f-508c-9e6f-d87756cc2771" "answer-1dbfd70f-5e32-5f4c-9459-b0ae4b834535" "answer-8d9d7b6b-6fdb-5ed5-bcb4-eab5156b4447" "answer-f79f2a31-fef1-5434-90a8-26e88176d330" "answer-475c219c-d8f4-5ecb-aef0-762429b48a5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8085e5d-331f-508c-9e6f-d87756cc2771" :answer/id #uuid "b8085e5d-331f-508c-9e6f-d87756cc2771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dbfd70f-5e32-5f4c-9459-b0ae4b834535" :answer/id #uuid "1dbfd70f-5e32-5f4c-9459-b0ae4b834535" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d9d7b6b-6fdb-5ed5-bcb4-eab5156b4447" :answer/id #uuid "8d9d7b6b-6fdb-5ed5-bcb4-eab5156b4447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f79f2a31-fef1-5434-90a8-26e88176d330" :answer/id #uuid "f79f2a31-fef1-5434-90a8-26e88176d330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-475c219c-d8f4-5ecb-aef0-762429b48a5f" :answer/id #uuid "475c219c-d8f4-5ecb-aef0-762429b48a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2664ee6-8acb-52ad-889d-ed63a283e637" :question/id #uuid "b2664ee6-8acb-52ad-889d-ed63a283e637" :question/math-academy-id "q-103117" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\,1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯-\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(\\pi /8)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(\\pi /8)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{{8}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{{8}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =1-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{64\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{4}}{4\\,096\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{\\pi }^{2n}}{{8}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf45e113-afc9-589f-ba9f-87e14316c2aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf45e113-afc9-589f-ba9f-87e14316c2aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf45e113-afc9-589f-ba9f-87e14316c2aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-786f03b1-91d3-5f0b-98d1-31ea6b606b45" "answer-a132b4e2-4cf1-5445-83d6-b3de269c66b7" "answer-277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" "answer-de32adf5-d49b-5e95-96c0-dc0ee2551230" "answer-7f8df014-f766-508e-ae02-8b1cf949fa8c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-786f03b1-91d3-5f0b-98d1-31ea6b606b45" :answer/id #uuid "786f03b1-91d3-5f0b-98d1-31ea6b606b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a132b4e2-4cf1-5445-83d6-b3de269c66b7" :answer/id #uuid "a132b4e2-4cf1-5445-83d6-b3de269c66b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" :answer/id #uuid "277698a4-b642-5828-bd44-26f327d9872a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de32adf5-d49b-5e95-96c0-dc0ee2551230" :answer/id #uuid "de32adf5-d49b-5e95-96c0-dc0ee2551230" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f8df014-f766-508e-ae02-8b1cf949fa8c" :answer/id #uuid "7f8df014-f766-508e-ae02-8b1cf949fa8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b7d68eb-3099-57db-9579-cc9c26274e37" :question/id #uuid "6b7d68eb-3099-57db-9579-cc9c26274e37" :question/math-academy-id "q-350681" :question/problem "What is the sum of the series $\\,1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{{(1/3)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(1/3)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{(1/3)}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}) & =1-\\frac{1}{9\\cdot 2!}+\\frac{1}{81\\cdot 4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{3}^{2n}\\cdot (2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $cos\\,(\\frac{1}{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e15e41c7-21f5-50db-bcda-4b29a0f68ef3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e15e41c7-21f5-50db-bcda-4b29a0f68ef3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e15e41c7-21f5-50db-bcda-4b29a0f68ef3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc" :answer/id #uuid "7aacd782-dbd4-58d3-8bc5-764458467ecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176979 :tutorial/content "We need to recognize when a particular series looks like a standard Maclaurin series. A list of some common Maclaurin series is given below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1}{1-x}=1+x+{x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}, &  & x\\in (-1,1) \\\\  & \\frac{1}{1+x}=1-x+{x}^{2}-⋯+(-1)^{n}{x}^{n}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(-1)^{n}{x}^{n}, &  & x\\in (-1,1) \\\\  & {e}^{x}=1+x+\\frac{1}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯+\\frac{{x}^{n}}{n!}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{n}}{n!}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\  & \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n}}{n}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n}}{n}, &  & x\\in (-1,1] \\\\  & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)=x-\\frac{1}{3!}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{5!}{x}^{5}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)=1-\\frac{1}{2!}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4!}{x}^{4}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this lesson, we will focus on recognizing the standard Maclaurin series for the sine and cosine functions.\n\n**Note:** To remember the series for $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$ easily, notice that they are both alternating series that contain every other term of the expansion for $e^x.$ Sine has the odd-degree terms (since it is an odd function), and cosine has the even-degree terms (since it is an even function)." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176122 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176693 :step/math-academy-id 649411 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176676 :step/math-academy-id 649412 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176677 :step/math-academy-id 649415 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
